  "caption": "Quinn was an undefeated jar opener, until one big twist left the little-finger side of the wrist sore.\n\nPain on that side of the wrist, worse with twisting or leaning on the hand, often involves the TFCC, a small cushion of cartilage and ligament. A fall on an outstretched hand, a forceful twist or lots of loaded rotation over time can irritate it, even without one clear injury.\n\nWhat often helps: neutral grips (fists or push-up handles), a pause on heavy loaded twisting, gradual forearm, wrist and grip strengthening, and bringing weight bearing back in steps. Rehab often takes 8–12 weeks.\n\nClunking, locking, numbness, a change in shape after a fall, or no improvement over a few months is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
